WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.210
- [Dr. Mike] Sunflower Bae.

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.044
So if you didn't know
already, we're married.

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:06.244
And I just want to know
how many kids we're having.

00:00:06.244 --> 00:00:08.109
(jaunty, cheerful music)

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:09.709
♪ Cha, cha, cha ♪

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.900
♪ Cha, cha, cha ♪

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.230
Sunflower, I think it
would take me meeting you

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.728
in order for us to be married
and having kids, right?

00:00:16.728 --> 00:00:18.880
I don't think we've met yet.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.696
(gasp)

00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:21.529
(laughs)

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:23.270
Hey guys, I'm back at it this week

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.957
reading and responding
to your YouTube comments.

00:00:25.957 --> 00:00:27.900
"So this must be a very stupid question.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.350
How often does a person
need to change undies?"

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.510
Mico, I would do it daily.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:37.510
Fungi love warm...
wet...dark environments.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.536
When you re-wear the same underwear,

00:00:39.536 --> 00:00:42.519
that fungus can start growing on your skin

00:00:42.519 --> 00:00:45.950
and you will get a condition
known as jock itch.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.960
Or, some women can get a yeast infection.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.527
So, Mico, change up that
underwear daily, please?

00:00:50.527 --> 00:00:51.360
"Hey, Dr. Mike."

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.257
Hey, Ruthie.

00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:54.550
"Apparently pollen season started already.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.030
I think a spring allergy
video slash pollen video

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.250
would be awesome.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.100
Since that is something
I've been suffering for

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:00.933
for about six years."

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:02.382
It's a little bit of a complex answer.

00:01:02.382 --> 00:01:06.770
For those patients of mine
who have springtime allergies,

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.040
there's definitely something to be said

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.290
about taking a daily
controller medication.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.658
There are websites you can
visit to see pollen counts,

00:01:13.658 --> 00:01:15.860
like the daily pollen
forecast for that day.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.057
There are days when the
pollen count is so high

00:01:18.057 --> 00:01:20.960
that a person like you
should not be outdoors,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.303
or should at least strictly
limit the time spent outdoors.

00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:25.052
Perhaps getting a filter for your home

00:01:25.052 --> 00:01:28.040
that is certified to
remove pollen from the air

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:28.873
would be ideal.

00:01:28.873 --> 00:01:31.247
"Would you wear a shirt with
a few buttons left undone

00:01:31.247 --> 00:01:34.200
when you (laughing)
publish your next video?

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.544
I think you would get more views."

00:01:35.544 --> 00:01:38.000
Well Shawn, I appreciate the compliment.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.596
Yeah, uh, I would do that.

00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:41.193
I have no problem wearing a shirt

00:01:41.193 --> 00:01:42.560
with a couple buttons undone.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.850
I don't know how low you want me to go,

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.834
like those old school Russian gangsters.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:48.620
When I grew up--I'm
Russian--I used to hang out

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.930
at Brighton Beach, and the
guys would have their shirts

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:53.289
down to here, and I'd be
like what is going on?

00:01:53.289 --> 00:01:54.247
(fabric ripping) (gasp)

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.920
- [Dr. Mike] "What's the maximum frequency

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.750
that one should eat fish in a week?"

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.880
That's a great question, Omar.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.010
Are you eating wild
fish versus farmed fish?

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.247
Are you eating smaller
fish like tuna or salmon?

00:02:05.247 --> 00:02:08.030
Or are you eating large
fish like swordfish?

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.730
Larger fish, predator type of fish

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.760
generally have higher levels of mercury.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.420
I do think it's relatively safe to do like

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:17.560
three or four times a week
eating a tuna or salmon.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.140
Peachy Montoya.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.010
What a name.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.210
I don't know if that's your name

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.600
or your username, but it's awesome.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.680
I love peaches, by the way.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.054
That's why I'm obsessed
with Peach Snapple.

00:02:25.054 --> 00:02:26.617
(shushes)
(whispering) A lot of sugar.

00:02:26.617 --> 00:02:27.959
"Dr. Mike, how long will it take

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:30.210
for large stretch marks to fade away?"

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.245
Stretch marks, once they're
there, they're there.

00:02:33.245 --> 00:02:35.760
And while there are some laser procedures

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.117
and surgical procedures
that can get rid of them,

00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:40.800
it's very difficult, near impossible,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.780
to get rid of stretch marks
because it is scar tissue.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.180
It's basically damage that's
happened to your skin.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.240
How do stretch marks happen?

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.230
Well, your skin is naturally
somewhat elastic, right?

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.988
If I pull on my skin
here it just doesn't tear

00:02:51.988 --> 00:02:53.740
and rip and bleed, right?

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.290
But, if your body size changes rapidly,

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.500
you gain muscle too
quickly, you are pregnant,

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.740
you put on a lot of weight

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:01.970
because you've been eating poorly,

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.430
any one of those drastic changes

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.680
where the skin has to
adapt rather quickly,

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.190
you're gonna get some damage there.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.137
When you have damage, you get scar tissue.

00:03:09.137 --> 00:03:10.830
"Hey Dr. Mike, is it true alkaline water

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.590
better than regular water?"

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.200
Diana, I have never seen this to be true.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.520
I understand why some
people are promoting it,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.570
and I think it's based on flawed science,

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.330
or at least incomplete science.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.070
What you put in your body,
whether it's alkaline or acidic,

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.110
it doesn't change the
acidity of your blood.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.587
That's not how it works.

00:03:28.587 --> 00:03:30.460
"I was wondering if you would have become

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.750
something other than a doctor,

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:32.710
what would it have been?"

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.850
Maggie, I would have been a detective.

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.940
I love investigating, and
putting pieces together,

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.040
and seeing little things that other people

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.814
don't see--little details,
like Sherlock Holmes style.

00:03:42.814 --> 00:03:44.990
And I think being a doctor is very similar

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.600
to being a detective, so.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.607
Lauren Garcia.

00:03:47.607 --> 00:03:49.760
"Does muscle really weigh more than fat?"

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.890
Well, that's like the
typical trick question

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:52.723
that people ask.

00:03:52.723 --> 00:03:54.114
What weighs more: a pound of feathers,

00:03:54.114 --> 00:03:55.620
or a pound of gold?

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.610
They weigh the same.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.260
Muscle doesn't weigh more than fat,

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.890
and fat doesn't weigh more than muscle.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.780
Now, that being said,
muscle is more dense.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:05.530
So, it would look like less muscle

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.800
is needed to weigh the same as more fat

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.420
'cause fat is less dense.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.040
But in reality, one pound of muscle

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.227
equals one pound of fat.

00:04:12.227 --> 00:04:14.050
"What do you think of
cranberry supplements?

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.890
Do they really prevent UTIs?"

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.600
Well, Andrea, I'll tell you this:

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.220
cranberry supplements, the way
that they're supposed to work

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.370
is that they're supposed
to acidify your urine.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:25.390
When you acidify your urine
it makes it less likely,

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.960
or supposedly makes it less likely

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.150
that you'll get an infection,

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.950
'cause bacteria don't like to
live in an acidic environment.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.290
That's the premise behind
taking cranberry supplements.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.910
Number one, I don't like supplements.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.170
So I would much rather you just
have (laughing) cranberries

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.060
or drink cranberry juice.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.820
Natural stuff, not the concentrate.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.890
The evidence, honestly,
like I've looked at it,

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.160
it's fairly weak.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.759
But again, because we look
at harms versus benefits

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:49.640
in these types of situations

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.900
I think the benefits
probably outweigh the harms.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.310
If there's even a slight chance

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.070
that cranberries can help your UTI

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:57.110
or prevent a UTI,

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.800
go eat some cranberries.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.820
Because, what's the harm
in eating some cranberries?

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.410
They're rich in antioxidants,

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.690
and if they help prevent UTIs, boom.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.207
You've got yourself a two in one deal.

00:05:06.207 --> 00:05:08.420
"Dr. Mike, I think you would look good

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:10.890
with (laughing) bleach-blonde hair.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.700
This wasn't a request, it's a demand."

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:14.533
Chill!

00:05:14.533 --> 00:05:16.719
Beach-blonde hair...

00:05:16.719 --> 00:05:19.100
(laughing) I think I'd look
really weird, I don't know.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.490
Maybe if we get this
video to 200,000 likes

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.896
I'll dye my hair blonde.

00:05:22.896 --> 00:05:24.260
(muffled) Oh my god, I probably
shouldn't have said that.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.800
I didn't commit to that,
there was no handshake...

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.897
Don't get your lawyers involved.

00:05:27.897 --> 00:05:29.360
"Hey Dr. Mike, I have a question.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.620
Why is it that I always
get ear infections?

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.950
I clean my ears every
day, use nasal spray,

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.810
and sleep on a heating pad each night."

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.299
Okay, Emma, you make one
of the biggest mistakes

00:05:38.299 --> 00:05:41.400
that my patients most often make.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.020
Cleaning your ears, I assume, with Q-Tips.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:46.070
Q-Tips, what they actually do,

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.620
number one, instead of getting earwax out

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.430
they just end up pushing the earwax

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.710
back into the ear and clogging it,

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.830
therefore making it more
susceptible to infection.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.330
The second thing they
do--because the Q-Tip,

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.290
the cotton is slightly rough,

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.120
and the area within
your ear is very gentle,

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.020
very sensitive,

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.420
when you put the Q-Tip in your ear

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.887
and scratch your ear, it may feel good.

00:06:05.887 --> 00:06:07.820
But what you're doing is you're creating

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.360
micro-tears, little
irritations in the skin,

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.087
that basically make it more susceptible

00:06:12.087 --> 00:06:14.606
for bacteria to get in there
and cause an infection.

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:17.420
So, by cleaning your ears
everyday with a Q-Tip

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.890
you're actually making it more likely

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.027
that you're gonna get an infection.

00:06:20.027 --> 00:06:22.490
"What are your thoughts
on colon hydrotherapy

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:23.550
and coffee enema,

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.160
and would you recommend these therapies?"

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.900
Melinda, no I would not.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.900
Never, in no way, sense,
or how of the word

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.740
would I ever recommend a coffee enema

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.450
or colon hydrotherapy.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.339
This is the definition of garbage.

00:06:39.339 --> 00:06:41.700
Please do not waste your money on it.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:44.760
As you can tell, my vein
is popping out right now.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.390
'Cause I'm quite angry that these people

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.790
are taking your money, and misguiding you,

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.510
and giving you lofty promises.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.517
Coffee enemas are B.S.

00:06:52.517 --> 00:06:55.250
Anyone who tells you that
they're good for your health

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.280
is a P.O.S.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.300
- [Woman] Just calm down.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.000
- [Dr. Mike] Sueda Gunes.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.210
I'm sorry if I said that wrong.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.547
It's--I don't know what
the double dots represent.

00:07:02.547 --> 00:07:04.870
"I already have black rings under my eyes.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:05.940
How can I get rid of them?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.730
People always assume that I'm sick."

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.630
So I think this is a great question.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:12.770
If you have a lifestyle where
you're not sleeping well,

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:14.450
where you're not well-hydrated,

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.993
if you eat too much salt,

00:07:15.993 --> 00:07:18.430
all of those things really affect

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.000
the area underneath our eyes.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.160
Because of the bone formation
surrounding our eyes,

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.740
the skin is very thin.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.487
And the way that the light reflects

00:07:26.487 --> 00:07:29.670
from light that's generally
above us, in this area,

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.400
can make it seem darker
than it actually is.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.270
Also, because this skin is thinner,

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.820
you can generally see
more blood vessels there.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.170
And blood vessels being veins,

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:41.270
and veins are generally a bluish color,

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.800
how the light reflects off that area

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.620
can seem darker or blacker
than the rest of your skin.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.680
First and foremost,
what I would recommend:

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.320
make sure you're getting enough sleep.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.330
Make sure you're eating a healthy diet,

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.870
not over-eating salt, and
you're staying well-hydrated.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.510
Get your exercise in, because
I say it all the time,

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.650
exercise is basically a cure-all

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.010
that helps with almost
every aspect of our lives.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.890
Finally, if you're still
unhappy with your appearance

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:05.000
there are some cosmetic things you can do.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.270
There are bleaching creams

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.310
if it's a--seriously a color issue.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:10.557
There's also injections that you can put

00:08:10.557 --> 00:08:12.589
right below the eye here

00:08:12.589 --> 00:08:14.716
which basically act as a filler.

00:08:14.716 --> 00:08:17.799
It basically lifts the
skin up off of the bone,

00:08:17.799 --> 00:08:20.410
and it changes the way the light reflects

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.680
off of the area.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:24.677
And therefore the area seems
more full, and less dark.

00:08:24.677 --> 00:08:26.470
"Hey, so I'm a sophomore in high school

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.280
and I'm super interested
in the medical field.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:30.640
Do you have any recommendations
for classes I should take?

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.530
Your videos are great."

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.940
I don't think in high school you should

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.617
specialize your classes to
get you ready for med school,

00:08:36.617 --> 00:08:37.960
and I'll explain why.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:40.240
In college, you're already gonna be forced

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.250
to take a specific set of courses

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.770
if you wanna get into medical school.

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:44.900
And then once you're in medical school,

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:46.120
obviously there's a curriculum.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.900
So you might as well spend
your time in high school

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.150
to try and learn as many different topics,

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.690
very broad categories,

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:54.839
so you can figure out
if med school is for you

00:08:54.839 --> 00:08:57.440
or maybe you're drawn to
something completely different

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.840
like politics or something.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.080
Even though right now the
political landscape is crazy.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.030
But, take a broad diversity of classes,

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:05.986
see what you enjoy, see
where your passions lie,

00:09:05.986 --> 00:09:07.503
and I think that's what's gonna make you

00:09:07.503 --> 00:09:09.020
a great candidate for medical school.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:09.853
Tom.

00:09:09.853 --> 00:09:11.360
"Do you wanna live in NYC your whole life

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.480
or move away in the future?
(high-pitched whine)"

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:17.140
I don't know why you added
the (high-pitched whine)

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:17.973
in there.

00:09:17.973 --> 00:09:20.100
(chuckling) I don't know,
I'm a New York City guy

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.250
ever since I moved here
when I was six years old.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.970
I've lived in Brooklyn, Staten Island,

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:25.750
Long Island, now in New York City.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.096
I love this place, I call
it home, my family's here.

00:09:28.096 --> 00:09:30.247
Roxy's here, Barry's
here, so I don't know.

00:09:30.247 --> 00:09:31.963
I think I'm staying here.

00:09:31.963 --> 00:09:33.460
If not for my whole life,

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:35.240
definitely for the foreseeable future.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.351
Good question, Tom.

00:09:36.351 --> 00:09:38.790
